Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:01.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like it's it's not just that.\N不只是这样。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.26,0:00:02.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like,\N就像是，
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.10,0:00:06.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,oh actually the model is committing many times or it's like trying to\N哦，实际上模型在反复提交代码，或者是在尝试
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.38,0:00:09.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,compile many times or it's trying to do unit tests throughout its agentic process.\N频繁编译，或者它在代理式流程中不断尝试单元测试。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.81,0:00:16.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, now that's that's increasing the frequency in which the generator, i.e. the model, is sending to the verifier.\N现在，这相当于提高了生成器，也就是模型，向验证器发送的频率。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.12,0:00:18.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and that loop gets tighter and tighter and tighter.\N而且这个循环变得越来越紧密。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.77,0:00:26.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And as we as we continue to move to more complex RL, it's like the model will actually uh be verifying its output constantly, right?\N随着我们不断迈向更复杂的强化学习，模型实际上会持续验证其输出，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.32,0:00:30.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like if you imagine um let's say models that are training over the next year or two is\N就像你想象一下，假设未来一两年内模型正在训练
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.81,0:00:35.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,is let's say a robot model that's verifying and that's that's in in a like a world model,\N比如一个正在验证的机器人模型，它处于类似世界模型的环境中。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.31,0:00:35.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.88,0:00:40.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,So uh VLM is is navigating across the world trying to pick up things, put them down.\N嗯，VLM 在虚拟世界里移动，试图捡起东西、放下东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.67,0:00:45.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every single action needs to be verified against the physics model that is sitting on some CPUs.\N每一项操作都必须与运行在某些 CPU 上的物理模型进行核对。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.50,0:00:53.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that's that's insanely way more CPUs than you need for say doing unit tests or running a math proof, right?\N所以，这比做单元测试或运行数学证明所需的 CPU 多出太多了，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.88,0:00:56.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when we look at like o1, that's like all it could do was math, right?\N当我们看 o1 的时候，它能做的就只有数学运算，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.90,0:01:04.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and as we look at like you know, sort of uh GPT-5.4 or Opus 4.6, like it's okay agentic software,\N嗯，像 GPT-5.4 或 Opus 4.6，它们作为代理式软件已经算可以了，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.69,0:01:08.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,but like as we move forward to the next stage of, you know, whatever's coming,\N但随着我们迈向下一个阶段，也就是接下来可能出现的任何事物，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.56,0:01:14.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's going to be models that can understand, oh, I need to tie my shoe and like when I tie it,\N它会理解：哦，我需要系鞋带，而系的时候要用多大力量，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.26,0:01:16.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,what's the strength strength, yeah. like what's the tensile strength?\N强度是多少？比如抗拉强度？
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.73,0:01:22.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,All these things like as to the the has to be calculated cuz the verifier is just generating, you know, what's the next step.\N所有这些都必须被计算，因为验证器只是在生成下一步该做什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.08,0:01:28.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but every step needs to be checked way more often and the intensity of that calculation for checking the step it goes up a time.\N但每一步都需要更频繁地检查，而检查这一步的计算强度也会随之增加。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.90,0:01:29.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.23,0:01:35.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,But there's also another thing and you probably know better than I is like the the the level\N但还有另一件事，你可能比我更清楚，就是那个程度
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.20,0:01:41.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,of the the the strength of the GPUs can handle in parallel a certain amount of CPUs boxes.\NGPU 的算力可以并行处理多少台 CPU 服务器。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.89,0:01:44.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so as we get next generations of GPUs,\N因此，当我们迎来下一代 GPU 时，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.98,0:01:54.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,I feel that they will be able to spin up manage or work on more CPUs than they do now which is another stressor on CPUs now.\N我觉得他们将能够启动、管理或处理比现在更多的 CPU，这也会给 CPU 带来新的压力。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.70,0:01:56.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I mean that's that's certainly the case, right?\N是的，那确实如此，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.61,0:02:00.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,GPU Well, GPUs are also just like getting way higher power, right?\NGPU，其实 GPU 的功耗也在大幅上升，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.26,0:02:04.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,So one GPU will equal many many more CPUs over time, right?\N所以随着时间推移，一块GPU将相当于众多CPU，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.94,0:02:10.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and GPUs are getting more expensive gen on gen on gen, whereas vCPUs are flat, slightly down.\N而且 GPU 一代比一代贵，而 vCPU 的价格持平甚至略有下降。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.04,0:02:11.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.56,0:02:14.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and so certainly it's a different scale, right?\N嗯，所以这确实是一个不同的规模，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.62,0:02:18.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like one Blackwell versus one Rubin, performance is up X.\N一块 Blackwell 对比一块 Rubin，性能提升了 X 倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.46,0:02:19.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Price is also up X.\N价格也上涨了 X。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.94,0:02:28.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um whereas, you know, you may buy last generation CPU, new generation CPU and there's 192 vCPUs in this gen and last gen was like 96, right?\N嗯，比如说，你可能买上一代的CPU，或者新一代的CPU，\N这一代有192个vCPU，上一代大概是96个，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.80,0:02:34.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,So now you've got way more CPUs, but the the price increase is equivalent to what you got in additional vCPUs.\N现在你的CPU数量多了很多，但价格涨幅相当于你获得的额外vCPU所带来的成本增加。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.58,0:02:39.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's like sort of yeah, the the ratio will grow in the favor of vCPUs,\N所以比例会向 vCPU 倾斜，
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.07,0:02:44.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,but the cost will be sort of also probably in the direction of CPUs, but not sure how much.\N但成本可能也会向 CPU 方向上升，不过不确定会升多少。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.68,0:02:44.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.02,0:02:51.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and also the other stressor on that and we've seen this with with larger customers when they have\N而且另一个压力源也存在，我们之前在大客户身上就看到过这种情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.44,0:02:56.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,like they don't they have like a time allotment for GPUs and they don't want their GPUs to be idle.\N他们好像有分配给 GPU 的时间配额，不希望 GPU 处于空闲状态。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.23,0:03:04.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,So they rather pay uh for warm pool running CPUs so that whenever tasks come from the GPU, the CPUs are they're hot.\N所以他们宁愿为持续运行的热池CPU付费，这样当GPU有任务过来时，CPU就已经处于就绪状态。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.56,0:03:06.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're essentially working, right?\NCPU 实际上已经在工作了，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.34,0:03:10.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,So they'll we we I say we cuz we do mostly CPUs are certainly the cheap resource.\N所以我们会说，因为我们主要做 CPU，这显然是成本较低的资源。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.74,0:03:13.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't know if we're cheap, but cheap resource for this.\N我不知道我们是不是便宜，但这个资源确实很便宜。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.08,0:03:20.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that spends more GPUs actually just because the cost of having an idle GPU is to is way more expensive, right?\N所以实际上会用更多GPU，因为让GPU闲置的成本要高得多，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.86,0:03:22.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it's actually like a really interesting point, right?\N是的，这实际上是个非常有趣的观点，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.80,0:03:26.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,The business model is like no one does I mean sure, there's on demand GPUs,\N这个商业模式——我是说，确实有按需 GPU，
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.79,0:03:32.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,but like Lambda has like 50,000 plus GPUs and only 4,000 of them are on demand, right?\N但就像 Lambda 有超过 5 万块 GPU，其中只有 4000 块是按需可用的，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.50,0:03:33.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And they're always sold out.\N而且总是卖光。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.67,0:03:35.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,So like no one really has on demand GPUs.\N所以其实没人真的拥有按需 GPU。
